<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The \(x\)-intercepts for function \(f\) are \((-4,0)\) and \((0,0)\). These points have an \(x\)-coordinate that makes the output value 0.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="5b09d861-2c42-4fc9-adac-3b0c9323c015" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
